@startuml M6-Search-Activity

' Search operation activity flow: from user query to ranked results
' Shows all steps: parse -> normalize -> lookup -> score -> rank -> display
' Includes decision points and data processing stages

!define BGCOLOR #F5F5F5
skinparam backgroundColor BGCOLOR
skinparam activityBorderColor #333
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam arrowColor #333
skinparam shadowing false

title M6 Search Engine - Search Operation Activity Flow

start
:User enters query
"javascript async";
:Parse query
(extract terms, filters);
:Normalize terms
(lowercase, remove special chars);
:Stem & generate n-grams;

:Look up term in
inverted index (M4);

if (Terms found?) then (yes)
  :Collect candidate
  documents;
  
  :Calculate TF-IDF
  for each document;
  
  note right
    Parallel: Also retrieve
    document metadata
    (stars, lang, topics)
  end note
  
  :Apply metadata boosts
  (language match, star count);
  
  :Combine scores:
  0.75 × TF-IDF + 0.25 × boost;
  
  :Sort results
  by score (descending);
  
  if (Apply user filters?) then (yes)
    :Filter by language
    and owner;
  else (no)
  endif
  
  :Limit to top K
  (usually 10) results;
  
  :Format results
  for display;
  
  :Return to user;
  stop
  
else (no terms found)
  :Return 0 results
  "No repositories found";
  stop
endif

note right
  Performance targets:
  - Simple query: <10ms
  - Complex query: <30ms
  - 100+ docs matched: OK
  
  Latency measured:
  Lookup: 1-2ms
  Scoring: 5-10ms
  Formatting: 1-2ms
end note

@enduml
